# CODEOWNERS — review ownership for the tapstate-cloud repository.
#
# Rules encoded here (checked by scripts/check-repo-structure.sh):
#   1. Every production path MUST have a named owner. The `*` fallback alone is
#      NOT ownership: a path is owned only when a rule other than `*` matches it.
#   2. The shared contract surface MUST be owned by BOTH sides of the contract:
#      the provider (Control Plane) and the consumer (published SDK / runtime
#      clients). A contract edit is therefore reviewed from both directions.
#   3. Every owner listed here MUST be a team or user that actually exists in the
#      organization. A handle that does not exist makes the rule inert (nothing
#      is requested and nothing blocks a merge) and is rejected by the structure
#      check.
#
# Precedence: GitHub uses the LAST matching pattern, so the more specific
# contract-surface rules are listed after the broader directory rules below.

# ---------- Fallback ----------
# Repository default owner. This is a safety net, not production ownership.
* @tapstate/dev

# ---------- Production paths ----------
/cloud-control-plane/   @tapstate/dev
/common/                @tapstate/dev
/helm/                  @tapstate/dev
/.github/workflows/     @tapstate/dev
/Dockerfile             @tapstate/dev
/pom.xml                @tapstate/dev

# ---------- Shared contract surface (provider + consumer review) ----------
# Contract fixtures: the wire-level truth the Control Plane (provider) emits and
# the Cluster runtime / Console clients (consumer) depend on.
/cloud-control-plane/src/main/resources/contract-fixtures/ @tapstate/dev @ply0011
# Published Java SDK: generated from the OpenAPI contract and consumed outside
# this repository, so the consumer side reviews it alongside the provider.
/client/java/ @tapstate/dev @ply0011
# OpenAPI contract: the external API promise this repository publishes.
/client/api/openapi.yaml @tapstate/dev @ply0011
